  "notes": "The PR swaps the whole database layer: Prisma (base) becomes a new SQLModel/SQLAlchemy layer with Alembic migrations (head). The base controllers move to an unused archive folder. Head's models, controllers and services are new code, and every module that uses them was rewritten to the new API. No shared API does the same work on both sides; the only common code is import or cosmetic changes plus a trivial helper. Base's Prisma layer would also need a generated client and a PostgreSQL server. Neither environment can import the changed code as it stands: base lacks prisma and head cannot import tux. I did not try to repair them. No workload was written and check.py was not run."
